5.6 Discussion of Comparative Results

The corrected analysis reveals a more nuanced picture than previous estimates. Under the baseline assumptions, T³ES-G achieves EIME parity with lithium-ion batteries (360 vs. 324 kWh/kg) but remains below the regenerative fuel cell (625 kWh/kg) when degradation effects are fully integrated. However, the LREE of 41.0 demonstrates a strong energy payback from local construction, and the AIE of 192 kWh/kg still exceeds the battery baseline.

This finding does not invalidate the concept but rather reframes it: the primary advantage of T³ES-G lies not in raw EIME superiority but in the decoupling of storage capacity from Earth-imported mass. The sensitivity analysis in Section 7 identifies the parameter regions where the EIME advantage becomes significant.

