6. Simulation Requirements

6.1 Mechanical System Dynamics

Phase 1: Hoist and Carriage Simulation

· Model the batch hoist system with full motor/generator efficiency maps.
· Include empty-carriage return dynamics and loading/unloading time.
· Apply degradation curve \eta_{\text{mech}}(n) = \eta_{\text{mech}}^{(0)} r^{n/1000} with r \in [0.90, 0.99].
· Simulate 10,000 cycles to determine true average round-trip efficiency.

Phase 2: Cable and Transmission Analysis

· Evaluate Zylon/Kevlar cable life under lunar conditions (radiation, UV, thermal cycling, abrasion).
· Compare cable hoist vs. rack-and-pinion vs. linear motor architectures.
· Include counterweight configuration in the efficiency model.

6.2 Mass Module Production

Phase 3: Excavation and Processing Simulation

· Model excavation energy as a function of depth, regolith properties, and tool design.
· Calculate total energy per module: E_{\text{block}} = E_{\text{exc}} + E_{\text{transport}} + E_{\text{proc}} + E_{\text{bag}} + E_{\text{form}}.
· Parametric sweep of excavation energy: e_{\text{exc}} \in [0.005, 0.02, 0.05, 0.1]\ \text{kWh/kg}.

Phase 4: Bag Mass and UV Degradation

· Determine minimum bag mass for 5,000 kg module at safety factor 5.
· Evaluate UV/radiation degradation and required spare bag inventory.
· Investigate in-situ basalt fiber production as alternative to imported geotextile.

6.3 Thermal Management

Phase 5: Radiator Sizing

· Calculate radiator area and mass for worst-case duty cycle.
· Optimize operating temperature vs. radiator mass.
· Evaluate PSR cold-sink utilization.

6.4 Geotechnical Stability

Phase 6: Shaft Wall Stability

· Model stress distribution in shaft walls: \sigma_{\text{wall}}(z).
· Calculate factor of safety: FS = \sigma_{\text{allowable}} / \sigma_{\text{actual}}.
· Determine required lining thickness and composition.
· Evaluate seismic and dynamic loading effects.

