Appendix A: Complete Mathematical Derivations

A.1 Fundamental Energy Storage Equations

A.1.1 Gravitational Potential Energy

The stored energy per mass module is derived from first principles:

E_b = \int_0^h F(z) \, dz = \int_0^h m g \, dz = m g h

where:

· m = module mass (kg)
· g = 1.62\ \text{m/s}^2 (lunar surface gravity)
· h = vertical displacement (m)

Derivation of Lunar Gravity:

The lunar surface gravity is calculated from the gravitational constant and lunar mass:

g_{\text{Moon}} = \frac{G M_{\text{Moon}}}{R_{\text{Moon}}^2}

g_{\text{Moon}} = \frac{(6.674 \times 10^{-11})(7.342 \times 10^{22})}{(1.737 \times 10^6)^2} = 1.625\ \text{m/s}^2

The value 1.62 m/s² is used throughout this work as the standard approximation.

A.1.2 Reference Module Energy Calculation

For the baseline module configuration:

m = 5{,}000\ \text{kg}

h = 150\ \text{m}

g = 1.62\ \text{m/s}^2

E_b = 5000 \times 1.62 \times 150 = 1{,}215{,}000\ \text{J} = 1.215\ \text{MJ}

Converting to kWh:

E_b = \frac{1.215 \times 10^6\ \text{J}}{3.6 \times 10^6\ \text{J/kWh}} = 0.3375\ \text{kWh}

Total Stored Energy:

E_{\text{total}} = N \times E_b = 2000 \times 0.3375 = 675\ \text{kWh}

A.1.3 Batch Energy and Power

For a batch of N_b = 14 modules:

E_{\text{batch}} = N_b m g h = 14 \times 5000 \times 1.62 \times 150 = 17.01\ \text{MJ} = 4.725\ \text{kWh}

Mechanical power during descent at velocity v = 1.0\ \text{m/s}:

P_{\text{mech}} = N_b m g v = 14 \times 5000 \times 1.62 \times 1.0

P_{\text{mech}} = 113{,}400\ \text{W} = 113.4\ \text{kW}

A.2 Efficiency Model Derivation

A.2.1 Component Efficiency Chain

The round-trip energy flow is modeled as a sequence of conversions:

Charging Path (Electrical → Mechanical → Potential):

E_{\text{potential}} = E_{\text{electrical,in}} \times \eta_{\text{PE}} \times \eta_{\text{motor}} \times \eta_{\text{mech,up}}

Discharging Path (Potential → Mechanical → Electrical):

E_{\text{electrical,out}} = E_{\text{potential}} \times \eta_{\text{mech,down}} \times \eta_{\text{generator}} \times \eta_{\text{PE}}

Round-Trip Efficiency:

\eta_{\text{RT}} = \frac{E_{\text{electrical,out}}}{E_{\text{electrical,in}}} = \eta_{\text{PE}}^2 \times \eta_{\text{motor}} \times \eta_{\text{generator}} \times \eta_{\text{mech,up}} \times \eta_{\text{mech,down}}

