This uses the stored energy (675 kWh) rather than the usable energy per cycle (448.9 kWh). The difference is whether the average round-trip efficiency is already accounted for.

Clarification: The correct formulation is:

E_{\text{usable,lifetime}} = E_{\text{stored}} \times N_{\text{cycles}} \times \bar{\eta}_{\text{RT}}

This gives:

E_{\text{usable,lifetime}} = 675 \times 10{,}000 \times 0.406 = 2{,}740{,}500\ \text{kWh}

This is the total electrical energy delivered to the load over the system lifetime, accounting for the average round-trip efficiency.

