A.8 Autonomous Infrastructure Efficiency (AIE)

A.8.1 Formal Definition

\text{AIE} = \frac{E_{\text{usable,lifetime}}}{M_{\text{imported}} + \lambda E_{\text{local,construction}}}

where \lambda is the infrastructure-equivalence coefficient, representing the imported mass cost of generating 1 kWh of local energy.

A.8.2 Justification of \lambda

The coefficient \lambda converts local energy consumption into an equivalent imported mass penalty. It is derived from:

\lambda = \frac{M_{\text{power system}}}{E_{\text{power system,lifetime}}}

For a lunar photovoltaic power system:

M_{\text{PV}} = 500\ \text{kg for 100 kW array}

E_{\text{PV,lifetime}} = 100\ \text{kW} \times 24\ \text{h} \times 365.25\ \text{days} \times 10\ \text{years} = 8{,}766{,}000\ \text{kWh}

\lambda = \frac{500}{8{,}766{,}000} = 5.7 \times 10^{-5}\ \text{kg/kWh}

However, this is for the power generation system only. Including balance-of-system components, deployment, and maintenance:

\lambda_{\text{total}} \approx 1 \times 10^{-4}\ \text{kg/kWh}

