B.2.2 Structural Stability Analysis

The shaft wall stability is evaluated using the Mohr-Coulomb failure criterion:

\tau = c + \sigma_n \tan(\phi)

where:

· \tau = shear strength
· c = cohesion (kPa)
· \sigma_n = normal stress
· \phi = internal friction angle

Lunar Regolith Properties:

Parameter Value Source
Cohesion c 0.1–1.0 kPa Apollo sample analysis
Friction angle \phi 30–40° Simulant testing
Bulk density \rho 1.5–1.8 g/cm³ Apollo cores

Vertical Wall Stability:

For a vertical wall of height h, the maximum stable height without support is:

h_{\text{max}} = \frac{4c}{\gamma} \tan(45° + \phi/2)

where \gamma = \rho g is the unit weight.

For c = 0.5\ \text{kPa}, \phi = 35°, \rho = 1.5\ \text{g/cm}^3 = 1,500\ \text{kg/m}^3, g = 1.62\ \text{m/s}^2:

\gamma = 1500 \times 1.62 = 2,430\ \text{N/m}^3 = 2.43\ \text{kPa/m}

h_{\text{max}} = \frac{4 \times 0.5}{2.43} \times \tan(45° + 35°/2) = \frac{2}{2.43} \times \tan(62.5°) = 0.823 \times 1.921

h_{\text{max}} = 1.58\ \text{m}

This indicates that a 150 m vertical shaft cannot stand unsupported. Significant lining is required.

Required Lining Thickness:

For a lined shaft, the required lining thickness can be estimated from:

t_{\text{lining}} = \frac{p_{\text{max}} \times r}{\sigma_{\text{allowable}}}

where:

· p_{\text{max}} = maximum lateral earth pressure at shaft bottom
· r = shaft radius (or half-width for rectangular shaft)
· \sigma_{\text{allowable}} = allowable stress in lining material

p_{\text{max}} = K_0 \gamma h

where K_0 is the at-rest earth pressure coefficient:

K_0 = 1 - \sin(\phi) = 1 - \sin(35°) = 1 - 0.574 = 0.426

p_{\text{max}} = 0.426 \times 2.43 \times 150 = 155.3\ \text{kPa}

For compacted regolith lining with \sigma_{\text{allowable}} = 5\ \text{MPa}:

t_{\text{lining}} = \frac{155.3 \times 10^3 \times 10}{5 \times 10^6} = 0.311\ \text{m}

A lining thickness of approximately 0.5 m is recommended for safety factor 1.6.

B.2.3 Shaft Excavation Sequence

1. Surface preparation: Level the site and install hoist platform foundations
2. Initial excavation: Dig first 10 m, install initial lining
3. Progressive excavation: Excavate in 10 m increments, installing lining as you go
4. Mass module production: Use excavated regolith to produce modules
5. Bottom preparation: Install bottom storage pad and drainage

