Appendix F: Optimization Framework

F.1 Problem Formulation

The optimization problem is:

\max_{m, h, N, v, N_b} \text{EIME}

subject to:

P_{\text{out}} \geq P_{\text{min}}

\sigma_{\text{shaft}} \leq \sigma_{\text{allowable}}

v \leq v_{\text{max}}

M_{\text{imported}} \leq M_{\text{budget}}

T_{\text{production}} \leq T_{\text{budget}}

E_{\text{usable}} \geq E_{\text{requirement}}

F.2 Design Variables

Variable Symbol Range Type
Module mass m 2,000–10,000 kg Continuous
Shaft depth h 50–500 m Continuous
Number of modules N 500–10,000 Integer
Hoist velocity v 0.5–3.0 m/s Continuous
Modules per batch N_b 5–50 Integer

F.3 Objective Function

\text{EIME} = \frac{E_{\text{stored}} \times N_{\text{cycles}} \times \bar{\eta}_{\text{RT}}}{M_{\text{imported}}}

where:

E_{\text{stored}} = N \times m \times g \times h / 3.6 \times 10^6

\bar{\eta}_{\text{RT}} = 0.92^2 \times \bar{\eta}_{\text{mech}}^2 \times 0.97

\bar{\eta}_{\text{mech}} = \frac{0.90 \times 1000}{N_{\text{cycles}} \ln(r)} \left[ r^{N_{\text{cycles}}/1000} - 1 \right]

M_{\text{imported}} = M_{\text{hoist}} + M_{\text{cable}} + M_{\text{carriage}} + M_{\text{PE}} + M_{\text{control}} + M_{\text{lining}} + M_{\text{radiator}} + N \times m_{\text{bag}} + M_{\text{spares}}

F.4 Constraint Functions

Power Constraint:

N_b m g v \times \eta_{\text{gen}} \eta_{\text{PE}} \geq P_{\text{min}}

Shaft Stability:

FS = \frac{\sigma_{\text{allowable}}}{\sigma_{\text{actual}}} \geq 3.0

Velocity Limit:

v \leq v_{\text{max}} = 3.0\ \text{m/s}

Production Time:

T_{\text{production}} = \frac{N \times (m/5000) \times 33.4}{P_{\text{production}}} \leq T_{\text{budget}}

Energy Requirement:

N m g h \times 0.665 / 3.6 \times 10^6 \geq E_{\text{requirement}}

F.5 Solution Methodology

The optimization is solved using:

1. Genetic algorithm for global exploration
2. Sequential quadratic programming for local refinement
3. Monte Carlo simulation for sensitivity analysis

