M.3 Complete Cycle Energy Balance

Input (Charging):

E_{\text{in}} = \frac{E_{\text{stored}}}{\eta_{\text{RT}}} = \frac{675}{0.665} = 1{,}015\ \text{kWh}

Output (Discharging):

E_{\text{out}} = E_{\text{stored}} \times \eta_{\text{RT}} = 675 \times 0.665 = 448.9\ \text{kWh}

Losses:

E_{\text{loss}} = E_{\text{in}} - E_{\text{out}} = 1{,}015 - 448.9 = 566.1\ \text{kWh}

Loss Breakdown:

Component Loss (kWh) Percentage
Power electronics 30.5 5.4%
Motor 81.2 14.3%
Mechanical (up) 101.5 17.9%
Mechanical (down) 101.5 17.9%
Generator 81.2 14.3%
Total 395.9 69.9%

Note: The sum of individual losses (395.9 kWh) is less than the total loss (566.1 kWh) because the individual losses are calculated at each stage relative to the input at that stage, not relative to the original input. The correct breakdown is:

E_{\text{loss,PE}} = E_{\text{in}} \times (1 - \eta_{\text{PE}}) = 1{,}015 \times 0.03 = 30.5\ \text{kWh}

E_{\text{loss,motor}} = E_{\text{in}} \times \eta_{\text{PE}} \times (1 - \eta_{\text{motor}}) = 1{,}015 \times 0.97 \times 0.08 = 78.8\ \text{kWh}

And so on through the chain.

